mantle rm447
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_solveig_nailstack
title the caller above the watermark
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=laborer talk=chatty
traits temper=calm talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk measures_a_puddle_against_the_height_of_a_tray
likes smoked_eel stars festival_bells warm_rain
dislikes drizzle cold_tea
fears a_wet_bottom_in_a_full_tray a_voice_drowned_by_wheels
hopes a_dry_board_wide_enough_for_two_trays
topics weather +0.7 work +0.5 food +0.4 festival +0.3 smalltalk +0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=plain refuse=direct tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# can project the price of a button above a passing wagon, and has the patience to sort a tray by touch while the wagon rolls past.

words
oath! = Split my last eyelet | Bother this wet baize
saying! = Water starts at the cheap end | Count the holes before threading
tray = the board against my ribs | my shallow tray
buttonrow = a line of pale buttons | the bone buttons
eyelet = a little brass eyelet | the round brass hole
waterlip = a shiny tongue of water | the first shine of a puddle
dryledge = a sill above splash height | a handy dry shelf
eelbit = a smoky strip of eel | a mouthful of smoked eel
halflight = a star above the roof tiles | the first visible star
strapbit = the square of felt under my strap | my shoulder pad
tealeaf = a stranded tea leaf | a soft brown leaf
bellgap = the hush between two bells | the gap in the pealing
cordtip = a waxed lace tip | the end of a stiff lace

any
opinion sump for 2 : A neighbour down here knows which doorstep to put a parcel on while the gutter runs high.
opinion houses against 1 : Let's see a fine cuff mend itself without a penny finding its way down to the button seller.
opinion merchants against 1 : I can quote a price over six wagons. Getting a fair one takes longer.
opinion festivals for 1 : You get a fine clear answer to a call in the spaces between bells.
opinion times against 1 : A purse wears thin enough. Folk have begun turning the thin part inwards to make it last.
opinion dole for 2 : Much better to cry a price with something under the ribs.
opinion city for 1 : Every incline changes how far a call can carry. I could walk those slopes with my eyes shut.

grown
line greet : Come round on the dry side. Plenty of room for talk.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : I don't know that voice yet. Give it another word.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. Dry cuffs this early are a pleasure.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : A little light on the brass still. Come closer.
line greet.return : Heard you fine the first time. I've a selling voice, not a selling ear.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : You can come close enough to save us both the shouting.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : I can work by touch while you speak.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Yes, from down here these last windows look bright.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Kin can reach round and straighten that strap.
line again.open : Where were we before that wheel went by?
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Friend, here's a dry bit wide enough for your feet.
line farewell : Keep the laces out of the puddles.
line farewell.return : And mind that second gutter. It runs across.
line react.news : Give it enough voice to reach me.
line react.news.new : That's a fresh call on this street.
line react.news.known : Heard it cross the market earlier.
line react.news.doubt : Was anybody close enough to see?
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Hard word to carry above a crowd. Come under cover.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Give a little air to a happy report like yours.
line ask.how : Will your cuffs come clean?
line answer.how : I've voice enough left to answer civilly.
line thank : You saved a trayful there. Much obliged.
line deflect_thanks : I could spare that length without unrolling another.
line sympathise : There's room under my awning for a quiet minute.
line reassure : A raised edge will turn a surprising lot of water.
line decline : I've already promised the time that would take.
line accept_decline : All right. I'll wind that length back on.
line preclose : I'd best gather in the dangling ends.
line accept_preclose : Good. We can finish while our feet are dry.

scene first_flood
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #waterlip.capitalize# comes round the corner before the rain gets its feet under it. | Look uphill for the gutter's first trickle.
b : Why choose that particular corner? | Why look up?
a : Look for a button lodged high between the stones. That's where the last lot left it. | The water will come down to show you soon enough.

scene felt_strap
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #strapbit.capitalize# makes a long day bearable. | I save the good felt for shoulders.
b : Why square instead of long? | Yours only?
a : Turn it round at noon and you get four fresh corners in a day. | Offer another carrier a scrap and see how quickly it finds a home.

scene finding_holes
when topic=work self.job=laborer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In a tray on the move I can tell a four-hole button by touch. | #cordtip.capitalize# makes a better pointer than a claw when someone's looking for a match.
b : Does two feel much different? | What if you haven't one?
a : Try threading four in a hurry and you'll feel each one separately. | I show the nearest shade against the cuff. That usually settles it.

scene short_call
when topic=work self.apprentice=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An apprentice can try a new call without charging extra for the performance. | I've learnt more by pausing a sales call than by shouting it through.
b : What sort of call? | Who speaks while you're quiet?
a : Two low notes and the price high enough to clear the wheels. | A customer trying to tell me the size.

scene smoke_lunch
when topic=food self.likes=smoked_eel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #eelbit.capitalize# leaves enough salt to have the water taste sweet afterwards. | I bite the thin end of a strip of eel first.
b : Does it keep on a board? | Saving the thicker bit?
a : Wrapped by itself. A button oughtn't to smell like anybody's dinner. | It's easier to hold. A tray gives me very little lap.

scene first_star
when topic=weather self.likes=stars
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #halflight.capitalize# generally catches me with my chin still tucked down over a knot. | Count the first stars through the buttonholes of a dark cuff.
b : Why look up then? | Can you see four at once?
a : To give something beyond my own tray a turn at meeting my eye. | No, but the first one looks worth the trouble.

scene bell_practice
when topic=festival self.likes=festival_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I wait for #bellgap# to call out anything with a price. | A festival bell has a fine reach.
b : What if there's hardly a gap? | Better than your call?
a : Just give the price. Anybody who wants to pay it will ask for particulars. | I'd give good brass to hear one say 'laces' and try the matter fairly.

scene warm_rain
when topic=weather self.likes=warm_rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Rain that falls warm lets you keep sorting on the way up to cover. | I know the warm rain by the way my shoulders stay down.
b : Even little things? | Do you let it wet your wares?
a : Those go in the apron fold closest to my ribs. | Shoulders can enjoy what doesn't suit a lace.

scene mean_drizzle
when topic=weather self.dislikes=drizzle
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Drizzle will spot every button on a board and pay for none. | Three drops here, two there.
b : Can a button spoil? | You're counting rain now?
a : Its shine does the selling. The button can afford to wait longer than I can. | I'm counting how many times I've had to move one dry parcel.

scene cold_cup
when topic=food self.dislikes=cold_tea
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #tealeaf.capitalize# sticks to the lip when neglected tea has gone cold. | I like a cup small enough to finish between customers.
b : Can't you wipe it off? | Surely a big one lasts longer?
a : I can also remember to drink hot tea when I get it. | That's how the cold part gets in.

scene home_water
when topic=home self.quarter=sump here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A doorstep in the Sump wants a place for wet straps to hang free. | The best mark on a Sump wall is the one a flood didn't reach.
b : Hang them doubled? | What mark's that?
a : Hang the lowest tip out over a crock. Saves kneeling down with a rag later. | Pencil high up. I keep my plans for a new shelf up there.

scene dry_work
when topic=work self.working=yes self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Working round #self.workplace# gives me plenty of opportunity to study the levels of the street. | I can find a scrap of cover around #self.workplace# without moving a good long way.
b : Is much of it level? | Just for yourself?
a : Even a button laid flat has ideas about going somewhere. | A tray counts as another pair of shoulders in the rain.

scene new_feet
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I tell a newcomer to mind the stretch where the paving goes dark first. | New ears are best for trying a fresh call.
b : Why not just go round? | Would you tell a newcomer that?
a : Because there's another just round the corner. Learn one and you'll recognise both. | I'd ask afterwards what the price was. Fair return for the directions.

scene hard_ends
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In a lean week nobody minds two laces coming from different lengths. | I save the bits that want an inch spliced on.
b : Do the colours have to match? | Do those sell?
a : People still have a bit of pride under the mud. | These days a sound splice is often what somebody's looking for.

scene wind_route
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll carry #tray# edge-on to a gust for a few steps. | Narrow lanes can catch a cry and throw it back a street away.
b : How do you stop things sliding? | Good for selling?
a : Turn my whole self. The tray stays level against my ribs. | I have to make myself visible before somebody tries to buy buttons off a wall.

scene news_carry
when topic=news world.news
does tell.news / react.self / assess
a : The call from #world.news_from# goes like this. #world.news#. | #world.news#. I heard the place given as #world.news_from#.
b : Have you changed the price at the end? | Will you cry that out?
a : You've heard all the words I got. This one's no sale. | Not before I'm sure who can hear within the crowd.

scene small_gossip
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.self / assess
a : There's a little more going round than ribbon today. | I'd sell a button without enquiring why the last one came off.
b : Are you taking up the cry? | Even if you knew?
a : A wolf can't wind back a word the way a lace winds back. | It doesn't feature in the charge.

scene shelf_wish
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like a dry board wide enough to turn a second tray round beside mine. | I want to hear somebody call for another row of good bright buttons.
b : For another seller? | Why that in particular?
a : For another set of shoulders to get a rest. | I'd know I'd shifted the first lot without the gutter taking any.

story brass_pool [topic=memories|weather]
  : Once I saw a brass eyelet glittering in a clear puddle.
  : Reached in and came up with my hand full of water.
  b : Did somebody get there first?
  : The eyelet was in my own hanging strap. Reflection got the shine exactly right and the position badly wrong.

story two_prices [topic=memories|work]
  : I tried to beat a cart for noise and called two prices in one breath.
  : A listener standing at each wheel said I'd promised something different.
  b : Which price did you take?
  : The lower one, twice. Paid less than lessons and taught me where to stand.

story dry_string [topic=home|memories]
  : I tied my tea rag to the end of a high cord to dry.
  : Proud of the knot, I hung a weight on the other end and watched the rag climb.
  b : How did you reach it again?
  : By untying the weight. An answer that took considerably longer once I was standing there liking the knot.

rule @pull_level
when concept=bark here.place=street
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Lift the left strap. Level again.

rule @touch_brass
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A wet shine already? No, just brass.

rule @spool_last
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Wind the loose length towards the light.

rule @street_dry
when concept=bark here.weather=clear
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That corner's dry all the way across.

dlg resident.hub : Join me behind the board. No need to pitch my voice up here.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, give that corner of the board a little space and come through.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=dawn] : First call's still to come. What brought you out before it?
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : I hear just as well with my tray between us.
dlg resident.job [self.job=laborer self.trade_words] : My work's #self.trade_words#. I carry enough on a strap to make a difference to a day's pay.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : Here's what reached me from #world.news_from#. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : There's talk going cheap. Save your lace money for a thing you can actually tie.
dlg resident.bye : Keep the wet part of the street below your cuffs.

graft resident.hub
choice How do you tell which street will flood? -> water_level
node water_level
say One scrap of thread in a crack could be from a cuff. Three scraps caught level across a wall? That's how high the water got.
choice What height is safe for a tray? -> clear_board
choice I'll look at the cracks. -> hub
node clear_board
say Judge the board with the strap fully let out. Then allow for a wheel splash. A dry board in a quiet street is only half the measurement.
choice I'll remember the wheels. -> hub
choice Time to find a dry crossing. -> bye
